# Portfolio Copy Rules

All headlines, descriptions, buttons, alt text, and metadata must sound like a person wrote them for hiring managers and clients.

## Required

- Ground every claim in real CV facts (roles, products, stacks, outcomes).
- Prefer short, direct sentences.
- Headings must carry a clear meaning. No vague labels like "My Journey" or "What I Do Best" unless the body proves it.
- One CTA label per intent site-wide (e.g. "View work" and "Hire me").

## Banned

- Em dashes (`—`) and en dashes used as flourish. Use a normal hyphen (`-`) or rewrite the sentence.
- AI filler: "passionate about", "seamless experiences", "leveraging", "cutting-edge", "robust solutions", "digital presence", "bring your ideas to life", "exceptional", "innovative solutions".
- Ellipsis spam (...), emoji decoration in UI copy, fake stats, placeholder contacts.
- Synonym stacking and hollow intensifiers.

## Voice

- Specific over generic. Name the product, stack, or result.
- Confident and plain. No sales-page drama.
- Match Talib's profile: Full-stack, Next.js, MERN, AI integrations, Shopify, CRM work in Lahore.
